780|# The read-only check of an engine other than codex (agy A17, widened in wave 18 - F09-1/F10-1;
781|# muse wave 23, D12): '' when nothing the
782|# review must not touch changed during the run, else the reason - the working tree (tracked
783|# or untracked files; the paths that changed), the collab directory (EVERY file under it,
784|# recursively: every task's stores and handoffs - outside the tree fingerprint; the run's own
785|# <task>/handoffs/NN-<prefix>-<slug>.* files and the .consult.* lock and recovery files
786|# excepted), the brief, an artifact. The check cannot tell who changed a file, so the text
787|# does not blame the reviewer (F09-3). Gitignored paths, submodules and files outside the
788|# repository stay unmonitored (README "Engines", F12) - and so do reads. $CollabShown: the
789|# collab directory as shown in front of its paths ('.collab/' inside the repository, ''
790|# otherwise). The closing words are the engine row's TreeNote (D11).
791|function Get-EngineTreeProblem {
792|    param($RevBefore, $RevAfter, [bool]$BriefChanged, [string[]]$ChangedArtifacts, [hashtable]$CollabBefore, [hashtable]$CollabAfter, [string[]]$OwnPrefixes, [string]$Engine, [string]$CollabShown = '')
793|    $cut = { param([string[]]$Names) $n = @($Names); $list = (@($n | Select-Object -First 5) -join ', '); if ($n.Count -gt 5) { $list += ', ...' }; "$($n.Count) file$(if ($n.Count -ne 1) { 's' }): $list" }
794|    $why = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[string]
